WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.160
- Excuse me, sir, do you have
a moment to save the children?

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.080
- I'm sorry, man, I'm running late

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.293
and I just don't have
time to chat right now--

00:00:05.293 --> 00:00:06.840
- I understand that, I understand that.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.830
It's just that every minute,

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.540
another child dies unnecessarily,

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.190
a child who could live a fruitful life

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.660
with the help of just one small donation.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.790
- Yeah, I don't have the time, sorry.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.400
- I understand that, it's
just all it takes is $1

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.667
to save a child.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:20.520
(donor sighs)

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.680
- All right, you know what?

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.520
Fine, you're right.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.620
Yeah, who doesn't wanna help a child?

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.180
Let's save five children.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.259
- Tommy!

00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:31.926
(tires screech)

00:00:37.056 --> 00:00:39.860
(dramatic music)

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:40.800
All right, come on, come on, come on.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.500
One, two, three, four, five.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.913
Not so fast, just five.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.820
(children crying)

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:48.720
Thanks a lot, sir.

00:00:51.018 --> 00:00:53.935
(children yelling)

00:00:55.615 --> 00:00:57.223
- Oh my God, I have another dollar.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.080
I have another dollar.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.430
Sir, I have another dollar.

00:01:00.351 --> 00:01:02.070
(upbeat music)

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.080
- Turns out it wasn't a ghost at all.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.440
It was my little sister
hiding in the basement.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.823
She was going, "Moo," making
the noises the whole time.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.980
- Oh shoot, I forgot his juice boxes.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.900
- Oh.
- I will be right back.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:25.830
You'll be all right with Zachary?

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:26.993
- I think so.
- Okay.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.513
- So Zachary!

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:38.610
You know I'm gonna be marrying your mother

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:42.350
and I'm gonna moving in soon and I just...

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.653
I'm so excited to spend more time with ya.

00:01:48.969 --> 00:01:50.160
(dog barks)

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:55.160
You know, I know that you had
a hard time with your father

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.682
and he spanked you.

00:01:58.682 --> 00:02:01.570
And I just want you to know

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.600
that's not gonna happen with me, okay?

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.263
And I promise I will never spank you.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:16.730
Oh, 'kay, that's okay.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:25.830
I know why you did that,
but I will never spank you

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:29.190
because I know that you still--

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:30.980
Oh, that's...

00:02:33.173 --> 00:02:35.940
(Charles laughs)
Yow!

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.744
I don't know that there's
anything I did to deserve that.

00:02:39.744 --> 00:02:40.880
Okay, this...

00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:44.670
(Charles laughs)

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.080
You!

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.843
Okay, I'm gonna be real with you.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:52.440
You can't go hitting people, all right--

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:57.213
Oh, oh, oh, I ain't coming
back for that fourth one.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.910
All right, so we done, we
got that out of our system?

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.823
'Cause I know that this,

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:07.713
this isn't you.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.677
Oh, I told you you weren't--

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.283
Oh, oh, come on, this!

00:03:18.103 --> 00:03:19.730
Oh why!

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:21.390
Oh what!

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:24.540
Oh, that's unbelievable.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.373
What did I do?

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:28.683
I'm the good guy.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.503
I'm the good guy, man.

00:03:34.211 --> 00:03:36.300
(Charles sighs)

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.753
Look, I'm never gonna spank you.

00:03:41.416 --> 00:03:43.116
I'm not gonna be like your father.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.203
I'm gonna be your friend.

00:03:51.465 --> 00:03:54.504
You need to respect me, you understand?

00:03:54.504 --> 00:03:57.671
You little (beeping)!

00:04:04.991 --> 00:04:07.658
(Zachary claps)

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:17.600
- I will respect you, Charles,
if you play your role.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:20.223
Now, listen up.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.873
I'm a bad, bad boy, Charles.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.563
I don't need a (beeping) friend.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:33.220
So go ahead, marry my mommy, move in,

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.580
(beeping) her as hard as you want.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:38.253
Just leave me the (beeping) alone.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.600
You do that, 11 years from
now, I'll be out of the house

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:47.283
and we won't have any problems.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:53.420
You don't and I will break you,

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.053
okay, Charles?

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:03.900
- How are we doing?

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:04.733
- I love him!

00:05:08.081 --> 00:05:12.757
(Zachary cheers)
(Zachary claps)

00:05:12.757 --> 00:05:14.090
- Dad, Dad, Dad!

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:19.770
- Hey, what's wrong, man?

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:21.315
- I was having a nightmare.

00:05:21.315 --> 00:05:23.583
- Aw, again?

00:05:26.894 --> 00:05:27.900
What, you wanna talk about it?

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.733
- I miss Mommy.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:34.050
- Hey, I know, I know.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.003
Me too, me too, pal.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.659
Come here, man.

00:05:39.659 --> 00:05:41.080
(child cries)

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:41.913
It's all right.

00:05:41.913 --> 00:05:42.840
Hey, it's okay.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.577
It's gonna be okay, shh, shh.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:48.750
- I just don't want anything
to ever happen to you.

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:49.860
- Happen to me?

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:53.220
Hey, come on, man, ain't
nothing ever gonna happen to me.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:54.053
- Really?

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:59.160
- Yeah, that's what I said.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:02.160
So yes, nothing ever gonna happen to me.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:03.270
You ain't never gonna have to worry

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:04.650
about nothing happening to me.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:08.853
- But what if you got hit
by a car or something?

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:14.880
- That's impossible
because I will never die,

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:19.620
so I can't die, no matter what.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:21.240
- You can't die?

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.823
But I thought all human beings died.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.350
- That's true, that's true.

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:32.400
That's science, so that's
true, but I am lucky

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.310
'cause I'm not a human.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.360
- [Child] You're not?

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:39.344
- I never told you about this?

00:06:39.344 --> 00:06:40.177
- No.

00:06:41.392 --> 00:06:42.330
- You know, I'll just let it out.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:46.710
I'm from a planet called Thelonius.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.590
The thing is it was being destroyed.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:50.670
- Oh, all right.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:52.590
- That's what happened.

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:57.590
I was sent down here in a
capsule to earth by my parents.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:59.850
- Oh, like Superman?

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.250
- Superman, yep.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:05.970
That is what it is exactly like, except...

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.980
Oh, here's the thing about my version,

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:10.690
only one super power, immortality.

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:11.523
- Oh.

00:07:11.523 --> 00:07:13.140
- Yeah, so I'm tired.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.210
Daddy's tired.

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:16.770
Can you...

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:18.147
Let's go to sleep, okay?

00:07:18.147 --> 00:07:20.160
- But I'm not gonna live forever, right,

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:23.104
because I'm only half alien.

00:07:23.104 --> 00:07:24.154
(child cries)
Oh no!

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:26.883
So I'm gonna die.

00:07:27.734 --> 00:07:29.340
- Mm-hm, mm-hm, mm-hm, you?

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:36.495
You right about yourself, but...

00:07:36.495 --> 00:07:37.650
(Dad laughs)

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:41.340
Here it is, this one slipped my mind.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:46.340
You can build with me
immortality, the machine,

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:51.210
to give you what I got from
the remnants of my spacecraft.

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:54.720
So yeah, you gonna be immortal.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:56.190
You gonna be immortal.

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:58.390
- Daddy, when are we
gonna get the remnants?

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:00.083
- Tomorrow.

00:08:00.083 --> 00:08:01.175
- [Child] Tomorrow!

00:08:01.175 --> 00:08:02.820
(child gasps)

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:05.493
- Gonna get them tomorrow during work.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:09.150
- Hey, you got anything
that looks like parts

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:11.340
of a crashed spaceship?

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:12.347
- Dead mom?

00:08:12.347 --> 00:08:14.493
- Mm-hm.
- Mm-hm, right this way.

00:08:15.888 --> 00:08:18.471
(upbeat music)

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.370
- Nobody likes you, you girl!

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:26.370
- Well, you're a different
color than me and that's bad.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:27.203
- Oh yeah?

00:08:27.203 --> 00:08:28.710
Well, you dress like a--

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:31.375
- Now, hold on a second!

00:08:31.375 --> 00:08:33.750
- Whoa, Mr. T!
- Whoa, Mr. T!

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:35.700
- Never make fun of a way a man dresses.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.910
Way a man dresses is his business.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:41.850
Remember that, whether
it's overalls, chains

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:44.250
or feather earrings, however they dress,

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:45.870
it's not to be joked about.

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:48.603
I pity the fool that judges
another man's clothing.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.893
- I'm sorry I judged your clothing.

00:08:52.893 --> 00:08:54.003
- It's okay.

00:08:55.338 --> 00:08:57.921
(upbeat music)

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:03.060
- Hey, Scout, there's a man over there

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.100
who said he'll give us
candy if we get in his van.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.680
- Oh, I don't know if
that's a good idea, Timmy.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:09.990
- Oh, what are you afraid of?

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:12.420
Is it because you have a
stupid name, like Scout?

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:13.664
- Hey!

00:09:13.664 --> 00:09:16.470
- Whoa, Mr. T again!
- Whoa, Mr. T again!

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:18.210
- Never make fun of a person's name.

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:19.860
Your mama gave you that name

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:22.260
or you made it up for business purposes.

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:24.480
Either way, it's personal.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:26.850
I pity the fool that make
fun of another man's name.

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:28.380
Mr. T's a cool name.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.943
It's a cool name, Mr. T!

00:09:31.826 --> 00:09:34.409
(upbeat music)

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.010
- Hey, Scout, wanna do some drugs?

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.333
- Aren't drugs bad?

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:41.073
- I don't know.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.430
If you're afraid of drugs,

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:49.620
we could drink a bunch of alcohol.

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:51.393
- Yum, that sounds good.

00:09:53.124 --> 00:09:55.874
(birds chirping)

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.390
- Well, guess what, your hair is stupid.

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:03.060
- Never make fun of another person's hair!

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:04.770
- Hey, Mr. T!
- Hey, Mr. T!

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.420
- A person's hair is the artwork

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:08.580
that they present to the heavens.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.561
It's just like I've been saying.

00:10:10.561 --> 00:10:13.144
(upbeat music)

00:10:15.628 --> 00:10:18.198
♪ Hair ♪

00:10:18.198 --> 00:10:22.074
♪ It isn't fair ♪

00:10:22.074 --> 00:10:25.294
♪ Beware ♪

00:10:25.294 --> 00:10:30.294
♪ People care about their hair ♪

00:10:30.373 --> 00:10:33.658
♪ H is for the home where I lay my head ♪

00:10:33.658 --> 00:10:37.712
♪ And I cry about your
mean jokes in my bed ♪

00:10:37.712 --> 00:10:41.008
♪ A is for anxiety that fools provoke ♪

00:10:41.008 --> 00:10:42.842
♪ When they lookin' at my hair ♪

00:10:42.842 --> 00:10:45.124
♪ And they makin' jokes ♪

00:10:45.124 --> 00:10:48.303
♪ I is for I don't like the way I feel ♪

00:10:48.303 --> 00:10:52.537
♪ When you're joking that
my haircut does not appeal ♪

00:10:52.537 --> 00:10:55.738
♪ R is for the real mean jokes you make ♪

00:10:55.738 --> 00:11:00.537
♪ And the hurtful little
potshots that you take ♪

00:11:00.537 --> 00:11:03.780
And for your information,
it's not even a haircut.

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:07.733
It's a rare form of male
pattern baldness, you fools!

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:17.117
(Mr. T sobs)

00:11:24.501 --> 00:11:25.434
For real.

00:11:25.434 --> 00:11:28.017
(upbeat music)

00:11:29.772 --> 00:11:32.272
(light music)

00:11:52.641 --> 00:11:53.474
- Wow!

00:11:55.158 --> 00:11:57.658
(light music)

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:26.340
- Mrs. Whitaker, I have been
babysitting for 20 years.

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:27.420
I've seen it all.

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:31.080
- The thing is Forrest is a unique child.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:32.400
- Everything is gonna be fine.

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:33.960
I want you to have a good time tonight.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:35.490
You deserve it.

00:12:35.490 --> 00:12:38.880
- Okay, good luck.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:39.713
- Thank you.

00:12:49.284 --> 00:12:54.284
(dramatic music)
(footsteps tapping)

00:12:54.483 --> 00:12:56.650
- [Forrest] Goo-goo, gaga.

00:13:01.149 --> 00:13:02.700
- Oh!

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:04.113
Hey there, Forrest.

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:07.264
- Goo-goo, gaga.

00:13:07.264 --> 00:13:08.264
I want, I want milk.

00:13:11.127 --> 00:13:12.930
- You want me to get
you your bottle, buddy?

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.573
- I want milk.
- [Sitter] Okay.

00:13:15.495 --> 00:13:18.766
(dramatic music)

00:13:18.766 --> 00:13:20.594
(footsteps tapping)

00:13:20.594 --> 00:13:22.011
- This is a baba.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:25.650
I want Mama's milk.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:27.100
Why can't I have Mama's milk?

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:30.600
It's a simple request.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:34.830
- Yeah, well, you can't have
Mama's milk right now, buddy.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.420
How about we play?

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:41.420
- Okay, I want, I want, I
want to play with my Legos.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:42.930
- Okay, yeah.

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:46.530
Okay, buddy, let's get your Legos, then.

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:51.000
- I want, I want put the
smallest Lego in my mouth.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:52.007
That's what I'm gonna do.

00:13:52.007 --> 00:13:53.430
- No, no, you can't do that.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.020
- What?

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:57.780
First you tell me I
can't have Mama's milk.

00:13:57.780 --> 00:14:01.470
Now, you can't have my
smallest Lego in my mouth?

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:03.090
What a night.

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:04.413
This is a bad start.

00:14:05.298 --> 00:14:07.470
- Right, but Forrest, it's dangerous.

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:09.030
- Let me get this straight.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:11.850
You're in charge of me in my house?

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:13.530
- All right, Forrest, it's time for bed.

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:16.533
- I guess then you gonna sing me a song.

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:18.323
- What?

00:14:18.323 --> 00:14:21.360
- Mama always sing me a
song before we go to sleep.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:23.760
Are you gonna do that for me?

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:26.253
- Okay, okay, yeah, yes, I will.

00:14:28.132 --> 00:14:32.130
♪ Hush little baby, don't say a word ♪

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:34.479
- Keep, keep singing.

00:14:34.479 --> 00:14:38.040
♪ Mama's gonna buy you a mockingbird ♪

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:40.170
- Put my name in it.

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:42.906
I like, I like it personal.

00:14:42.906 --> 00:14:47.640
♪ Hush baby Forrest
Whitaker, don't say a word ♪

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:49.124
- Goo-goo, gaga.

00:14:49.124 --> 00:14:52.590
♪ Mama's gonna buy you a mockingbird ♪

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:54.104
- Good babysitter.

00:14:54.104 --> 00:14:57.080
♪ And if that mockingbird don't sing ♪

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.810
- Have a good cry

00:15:00.047 --> 00:15:04.547
♪ Mama's gonna buy you a diamond ring ♪

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:10.623
- Hi, you must be Liam.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:13.953
- Hey, buddy, how are you feeling today?

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:19.327
- I'm feeling fine, Dr. Gupta, just fine.

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:22.680
- This is Marian Glass,

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:25.080
she's from the Make-A-Wish Foundation.

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:26.463
- Marian Glass.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:29.883
- How are you feeling today, Liam?

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:32.823
- I'm fine, Marian Glass.

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:35.070
- Okay, well, I have some news

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.203
that might make you feel a little better.

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:41.130
We at the Make-A-Wish
Foundation make dreams come true

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:44.670
for little boys and little
girls who are very sick,

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:46.294
just like you.

00:15:46.294 --> 00:15:50.994
- There are no children
like me, Marian Glass.

00:15:50.994 --> 00:15:53.040
- Oh no, of course not.
- Of course not.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:54.210
- You're one of a kind,

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:56.190
but we're gonna make any dream come true

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:58.470
that you could ever have, okay?

00:15:58.470 --> 00:15:59.820
- Anything?

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:02.280
- That's right, buddy, that's right.

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:05.180
Would you like to play with
your favorite basketball team?

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:10.770
What about be Superman for a day?

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:14.296
- I wish to drown a man.

00:16:14.296 --> 00:16:17.046
(dramatic music)

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:19.534
- What?

00:16:19.534 --> 00:16:23.227
- To drown a man in the
bathtub, to hold him down

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:28.200
while the last breath escapes his body

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:31.020
and then bathe in that water,

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:34.377
all the while singing la la, la la, la la.

00:16:39.236 --> 00:16:40.069
- Liam!

00:16:41.427 --> 00:16:42.543
- You said anything.

00:16:45.510 --> 00:16:47.430
- Surely, we don't want
to hurt other people,

00:16:47.430 --> 00:16:49.637
now, do we, kiddo?

00:16:49.637 --> 00:16:50.490
(Gupta laughs)
(Marian laughs)

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:55.440
Anything else, fly in a hot air
balloon or meet a celebrity?

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:59.910
- My new wish is to lean
over the body of a dying man

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:04.712
and put my lips on his,
stealing his last breath.

00:17:04.712 --> 00:17:05.610
(Liam inhales)

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:06.900
- [Gupta] Liam!

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:08.787
- No one will get hurt.

00:17:08.787 --> 00:17:10.323
- No, absolutely not.

00:17:11.263 --> 00:17:12.313
I don't even know where you--

00:17:12.313 --> 00:17:17.313
- I wish to take all the
prosthetic legs in the hospital

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:22.700
and bind them together with
the dried flesh of the dead

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:28.430
into a webbed massive creature.

00:17:28.568 --> 00:17:29.401
- Liam!

00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:32.850
I am so sorry, Ms. Glass.

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:35.610
- It's all right, he doesn't
know what he's saying.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:37.260
- I wish to pee in your mouth.

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:38.093
- What!

00:17:38.093 --> 00:17:38.926
- Both of you.

00:17:38.926 --> 00:17:40.290
- Mine?

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:41.760
- Especially you.

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:42.593
- Oh.

00:17:42.593 --> 00:17:47.310
- I wish to pee in both of your
mouths as I stand over you.

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:49.800
I'll need a glass of water and 10 minutes.

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:51.150
- Enough, you little (beeping)!

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:52.590
- Dr. Gupta!

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:55.782
- No, you're reprehensible.

00:17:55.782 --> 00:17:57.510
You are evil.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:59.373
You are a devil child!

00:18:00.323 --> 00:18:01.156
(Liam cries)

00:18:01.156 --> 00:18:02.670
- Dr. Gupta, he's not a devil child.

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:04.170
He's just a child.

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:06.390
You have no business
working in a pediatric ward.

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.696
- What?
I'm gonna report you.

00:18:08.696 --> 00:18:11.113
(Liam cries)

00:18:14.284 --> 00:18:18.662
♪ Shame on you, Gupta. ♪

00:18:18.662 --> 00:18:21.912
♪ Shame on you, Gupta. ♪

00:18:22.857 --> 00:18:25.403
You really upset Marian Glass.

00:18:27.328 --> 00:18:31.584
- This is insane.

00:18:31.584 --> 00:18:34.830
You've made me question
everything that I've ever believed

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:38.073
about the essential goodness of children.

00:18:39.716 --> 00:18:42.003
- Wish granted.

00:18:44.537 --> 00:18:46.893
(machine beeps)

00:18:46.893 --> 00:18:47.726
- Liam.

00:19:00.985 --> 00:19:03.358
(Liam laughs)

00:19:03.358 --> 00:19:05.346
- I am dying, though.

00:19:05.346 --> 00:19:08.690
(machine beeps)

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:10.470
(light music)

00:19:10.470 --> 00:19:13.893
- What does it take to
save a child in Africa,

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:18.250
to save them from the
violence, to save them

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:20.913
from becoming a child soldier?

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:27.650
What if I told you that all
it took was just one beard?

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:32.580
For the price of one costume
beard, you can save a child

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:35.883
from becoming another statistic,
another warlord's pawn.

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:37.853
Be safe.

00:19:39.355 --> 00:19:42.600
(light music)

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:45.543
That's right, just one beard.

00:19:46.463 --> 00:19:49.650
And for a little more,
you can get them a cane.

00:19:51.365 --> 00:19:53.865
(light music)

00:19:59.709 --> 00:20:01.259
- We are here for our children!

00:20:02.099 --> 00:20:04.849
(dramatic music)

00:20:09.762 --> 00:20:12.179
(jazz music)

00:20:21.337 --> 00:20:23.370
- These are all old people.

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:24.570
We are wasting our time.

00:20:26.290 --> 00:20:29.821
- Wait!

00:20:29.821 --> 00:20:32.571
(dramatic music)

00:20:46.231 --> 00:20:49.152
(commander whistles)

00:20:49.152 --> 00:20:52.311
Go, go!

00:20:52.311 --> 00:20:54.811
(light music)

00:20:58.967 --> 00:21:00.050
- Call today.

00:21:02.725 --> 00:21:07.392
♪ We'll put a beard on an African child ♪

00:21:08.807 --> 00:21:11.390
(upbeat music)

00:21:13.783 --> 00:21:16.137
♪ Oh, I want you ♪

00:21:16.137 --> 00:21:18.063
♪ But I don't need ya ♪

